  "worked_solution": "Notice that the line and curve intersect twice, so we are expecting two solutions.\n\nTo find the coordinates of the intersection points, we take the equation of the line, replace $x$ and $y$ with the parametric formulas, and then solve for $t.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-y+4 & =0 \\\\ (-{t}^{2})-(-3t)+4 & =0 \\\\ -{t}^{2}+3t+4 & =0 \\\\ -(t+1)(t-4) & =0 \\\\ t & =-1,4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
